.. _strategies:

Strategies
==========

`pyreflow` has many options controlling its behavior when reading FCS files.

Since most users likely will not care about these options, an additional flag
called ``strategy`` may be used to set many flags in bulk.

Available strategies are:

* **strict (default)**: All options are at their default values. Only
  perfect FCS files will parse without error.
* **scalpel**: Parse and repair FCS file while attempting to preserve metadata.
  Non-trivial metadata such as whitespace around keyword values may be stripped.
* **sledgehammer**: Parse FCS file and do whatever is needed to parse *DATA*;
  possibly ignore/throw away metadata and non-*DATA* segments if their format
  cannot be determined.

Most users will likely want the ``scalpal`` strategy.

Those wishing for more control can fine-tune options after setting a strategy
(the easiest way to do this is via the pydantic interface, see
:ref:`config_interfaces`).

Scope and Limitations
+++++++++++++++++++++

Strategies are vendor-agnostic. Any values that are often used by a given
machine are not taken into account.

One place this matters is the treatment of the time measurement. The standard
dictates that the name of the time channel is ``"Time"`` (case-insensitive
matching recommended). However, some machines call this measurement ``"HDR-T"``
or ``"T1"``. `pyreflow` currently has no mechanism to determine what this value
should be; therefore, the user must supply the value themselves as necessary.

